/-!
# The relative Alexander grading of a doubly pointed diagram

A knot `K` in a closed `3`-manifold `Y` is presented by a doubly pointed Heegaard diagram
`(Σ, α, β, w, z)`: `(Σ, α, β, w)` is a pointed Heegaard diagram of `Y`, and `K` is the union of
an arc from `w` to `z` in the complement of the `α`-curves and an arc from `z` to `w` in the
complement of the `β`-curves, pushed into the two handlebodies. The knot Floer complex is generated
by the generators of the diagram of `Y`, and carries the *relative Alexander grading*

`A(x) - A(y) = n_z(D) - n_w(D)`

for a domain `D` from `x` to `y`, where `n_w` and `n_z` are the multiplicities at the two
basepoints. The differential of the knot Floer complex `CFK^∞`, generated by triples `[x, i, j]`
with `A(x) = j - i`, sends `[x, i, j]` to the triples `[y, i - n_w(D), j - n_z(D)]` over the
domains `D` of holomorphic disks from `x` to `y`, which preserves `j - i - A`. The hat
differential of `CF̂(Y)` counts nonnegative domains avoiding `w`, so it does not increase `A`: the
Alexander grading is a filtration of `CF̂(Y)`, whose associated graded complex is `CFK̂`, with
homology `HFK̂`.

This file develops the relative Alexander grading for the incidence data
`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem` with a single basepoint, which plays the role of `w`; the second
basepoint `z` enters only through the region `z : Region` containing it. Two domains from `x` to
`y` differ by a domain from `x` to `x`, which is a periodic domain `P` plus a multiple of the whole
surface. The whole surface has the same multiplicity at `w` and `z`, and `n_w(P) = 0`, so the two
values of `n_z - n_w` differ by `n_z(P)`. The grading is therefore well defined modulo the
subgroup `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.periodicMultiplicities` of the multiplicities `n_z(P)` of
the periodic domains, and on the nose when they all vanish. On a geometric diagram `n_z(P)` is
the intersection number of `K` with the class `H(P) ∈ H₂(Y; ℤ)` of the periodic domain (not
formalized here), so they all vanish when `K` is null-homologous, and in particular when
`b₁(Y) = 0`, when the only periodic domain is zero.

The value `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.relativeAlexanderGrading` computed from a chosen domain
is a representative of this class; it is additive and antisymmetric modulo the subgroup.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.periodicMultiplicities`: the subgroup of `ℤ` of multiplicities
  of the periodic domains at a region.
* `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.relativeAlexanderGrading`: the relative Alexander grading
  `A(x) - A(y)`, computed from a chosen domain from `x` to `y`, or `0` when there is none.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.IsDomainBetween.coe_relativeAlexanderGrading_eq`: modulo the
  periodic multiplicities at `z`, the relative Alexander grading is `n_z(D) - n_w(D)` for every
  domain `D` from `x` to `y`.
* `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.IsDomainBetween.coe_relativeAlexanderGrading_add` and
  `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.IsDomainBetween.coe_relativeAlexanderGrading_swap`: additivity
  and antisymmetry modulo the periodic multiplicities.
* `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.IsDomainBetween.relativeAlexanderGrading_eq`: when every periodic
  domain vanishes at `z`, the relative Alexander grading is `n_z(D) - n_w(D)` for every domain `D`
  from `x` to `y`; `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.IsDomainBetween.relativeAlexanderGrading_add`
  and `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.IsDomainBetween.relativeAlexanderGrading_swap` are its
  additivity and antisymmetry.
* `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.relativeAlexanderGrading_nonneg_of_mem_hatDomains`: the hat
  differential does not increase the Alexander grading.

## References

* P. Ozsváth and Z. Szabó, *Holomorphic disks and knot invariants*, Adv. Math. **186** (2004),
  [arXiv:math/0209056](https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0209056), §2: doubly pointed Heegaard diagrams,
  the relative Alexander grading `A(x) - A(y) = n_z(φ) - n_w(φ)` (Lemma 2.5 and its consequence
  for the filtration) and the differential of `CFK^∞`.
* J. Rasmussen, *Floer homology and knot complements*, PhD thesis, Harvard University, 2003,
  [arXiv:math/0306378](https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0306378), for the same filtration.
-/

public section

namespace TauCeti

namespace HeegaardRegionSystem

universe u v w

variable {n : ℕ} {Point : Type u} {Region : Type v} {Basepoint : Type w}
  {H : HeegaardRegionSystem n Point Region Basepoint}

section PeriodicMultiplicities

variable {z : Region} {P : Region → ℤ}

variable (H) in
/-- The multiplicities at the region `z` of the periodic domains, a subgroup of `ℤ`. With the
second basepoint of a doubly pointed diagram in `z`, the relative Alexander grading is well
defined modulo this subgroup
(`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.IsDomainBetween.coe_relativeAlexanderGrading_eq`). -/
def periodicMultiplicities (z : Region) : AddSubgroup ℤ :=
  H.periodicDomains.map (Pi.evalAddMonoidHom (fun _ : Region => ℤ) z)

/-- The periodic multiplicities at `z` are the image of the periodic domains under evaluation at
`z`. -/
theorem periodicMultiplicities_def (z : Region) :
    H.periodicMultiplicities z =
      H.periodicDomains.map (Pi.evalAddMonoidHom (fun _ : Region => ℤ) z) :=
  (rfl)

/-- An integer is a periodic multiplicity at `z` when it is the multiplicity at `z` of a periodic
domain. -/
@[simp]
theorem mem_periodicMultiplicities_iff {k : ℤ} :
    k ∈ H.periodicMultiplicities z ↔ ∃ P ∈ H.periodicDomains, P z = k :=
  AddSubgroup.mem_map

/-- The multiplicity at `z` of a periodic domain is a periodic multiplicity at `z`. -/
theorem apply_mem_periodicMultiplicities (hP : P ∈ H.periodicDomains) :
    P z ∈ H.periodicMultiplicities z :=
  mem_periodicMultiplicities_iff.mpr ⟨P, hP, rfl⟩

/-- The periodic multiplicities at `z` vanish exactly when every periodic domain has
multiplicity zero at `z`, the hypothesis of the `ℤ`-valued relative Alexander grading. -/
theorem periodicMultiplicities_eq_bot_iff :
    H.periodicMultiplicities z = ⊥ ↔ ∀ P ∈ H.periodicDomains, P z = 0 := by
  simp only [AddSubgroup.eq_bot_iff_forall, mem_periodicMultiplicities_iff]
  exact ⟨fun h P hP => h _ ⟨P, hP, rfl⟩, fun h _ ⟨P, hP, hk⟩ => hk ▸ h P hP⟩

/-- Periodic domains vanish at the basepoints, so the periodic multiplicities at the region of a
basepoint are zero. -/
@[simp]
theorem periodicMultiplicities_basepoint (b : Basepoint) :
    H.periodicMultiplicities (H.basepoint b) = ⊥ :=
  periodicMultiplicities_eq_bot_iff.mpr fun _ hP => (mem_periodicDomains_iff.mp hP).1 b

end PeriodicMultiplicities

open scoped Classical in
variable (H) in
/-- The relative Alexander grading `A(x) - A(y) = n_z(D) - n_w(D)` of two generators, for a
chosen domain `D` from `x` to `y`, or `0` when no domain joins them. Here `w` is the basepoint of
the diagram and `z` is the region containing the second basepoint. In a singly pointed region
system its class modulo the periodic multiplicities at `z` does not depend on the choice of `D`
(`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.IsDomainBetween.coe_relativeAlexanderGrading_eq`), and when every
periodic domain vanishes at `z` neither does the value itself
(`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.IsDomainBetween.relativeAlexanderGrading_eq`). -/
noncomputable def relativeAlexanderGrading (w : Basepoint) (z : Region) (x y : H.Generator) : ℤ :=
  if h : ∃ D, H.IsDomainBetween x y D then h.choose z - h.choose (H.basepoint w) else 0

variable {w : Basepoint} {z : Region} {x y v : H.Generator} {D D' E : Region → ℤ}

/-- When no domain joins `x` to `y`, the relative Alexander grading is `0`. -/
theorem relativeAlexanderGrading_of_forall_not_isDomainBetween
    (h : ∀ D, ¬H.IsDomainBetween x y D) : H.relativeAlexanderGrading w z x y = 0 := by
  rw [relativeAlexanderGrading, dite_eq_right (not_exists.mpr h)]

variable [Subsingleton Basepoint]

/-- In a singly pointed region system, a domain `E` from `x` to `x` has `n_z(E) - n_w(E)` among
the periodic multiplicities at `z`: it is a periodic domain plus `n_w(E)` copies of the whole
surface, which has multiplicity one in every region. -/
theorem IsDomainBetween.sub_mem_periodicMultiplicities (w : Basepoint)
    (hE : H.IsDomainBetween x x E) :
    E z - E (H.basepoint w) ∈ H.periodicMultiplicities z := by
  simpa using apply_mem_periodicMultiplicities (z := z)
    ((isDomainBetween_self_iff_sub_smul_one_mem_periodicDomains w).mp hE)

/-- In a singly pointed region system, the values of `n_z(D) - n_w(D)` for domains `D` from `x`
to `y` differ by periodic multiplicities at `z`. -/
theorem IsDomainBetween.sub_sub_sub_mem_periodicMultiplicities (w : Basepoint)
    (hD : H.IsDomainBetween x y D) (hD' : H.IsDomainBetween x y D') :
    D z - D (H.basepoint w) - (D' z - D' (H.basepoint w)) ∈ H.periodicMultiplicities z := by
  -- `D - D'` runs from `x` to `x`.
  have h := (hD.add hD'.neg).sub_mem_periodicMultiplicities (z := z) w
  rw [Pi.add_apply, Pi.add_apply, Pi.neg_apply, Pi.neg_apply] at h
  convert h using 1
  ring

/-- In a singly pointed region system in which every periodic domain vanishes at `z`, the value
`n_z(D) - n_w(D)` is the same for all domains `D` from `x` to `y`. -/
theorem IsDomainBetween.sub_eq_sub (w : Basepoint) (hP : ∀ P ∈ H.periodicDomains, P z = 0)
    (hD : H.IsDomainBetween x y D) (hD' : H.IsDomainBetween x y D') :
    D z - D (H.basepoint w) = D' z - D' (H.basepoint w) := by
  have h := hD.sub_sub_sub_mem_periodicMultiplicities (z := z) w hD'
  rwa [periodicMultiplicities_eq_bot_iff.mpr hP, AddSubgroup.mem_bot, sub_eq_zero] at h

/-- Modulo the periodic multiplicities at `z`, the relative Alexander grading is
`n_z(D) - n_w(D)` for every domain `D` from `x` to `y`. -/
theorem IsDomainBetween.coe_relativeAlexanderGrading_eq (w : Basepoint)
    (hD : H.IsDomainBetween x y D) :
    (H.relativeAlexanderGrading w z x y : ℤ ⧸ H.periodicMultiplicities z) =
      ((D z - D (H.basepoint w) : ℤ) : ℤ ⧸ H.periodicMultiplicities z) := by
  have h : ∃ D, H.IsDomainBetween x y D := ⟨D, hD⟩
  rw [QuotientAddGroup.eq_iff_sub_mem, relativeAlexanderGrading, dite_eq_left h]
  exact h.choose_spec.sub_sub_sub_mem_periodicMultiplicities w hD

/-- When every periodic domain vanishes at `z`, the relative Alexander grading is
`n_z(D) - n_w(D)` for every domain `D` from `x` to `y`. -/
theorem IsDomainBetween.relativeAlexanderGrading_eq (w : Basepoint)
    (hP : ∀ P ∈ H.periodicDomains, P z = 0) (hD : H.IsDomainBetween x y D) :
    H.relativeAlexanderGrading w z x y = D z - D (H.basepoint w) := by
  have h := QuotientAddGroup.eq_iff_sub_mem.mp (hD.coe_relativeAlexanderGrading_eq (z := z) w)
  rwa [periodicMultiplicities_eq_bot_iff.mpr hP, AddSubgroup.mem_bot, sub_eq_zero] at h

/-- A generator has relative Alexander grading zero with itself, modulo the periodic
multiplicities. -/
@[simp]
theorem coe_relativeAlexanderGrading_self (w : Basepoint) :
    (H.relativeAlexanderGrading w z x x : ℤ ⧸ H.periodicMultiplicities z) = 0 := by
  simp [(isDomainBetween_zero x).coe_relativeAlexanderGrading_eq w]

/-- The relative Alexander grading is additive modulo the periodic multiplicities:
`A(x) - A(y) + (A(y) - A(v)) = A(x) - A(v)` for generators joined by domains. -/
theorem IsDomainBetween.coe_relativeAlexanderGrading_add (w : Basepoint)
    (hD : H.IsDomainBetween x y D) (hE : H.IsDomainBetween y v E) :
    ((H.relativeAlexanderGrading w z x y + H.relativeAlexanderGrading w z y v : ℤ) :
        ℤ ⧸ H.periodicMultiplicities z) = H.relativeAlexanderGrading w z x v := by
  rw [QuotientAddGroup.mk_add, hD.coe_relativeAlexanderGrading_eq w,
    hE.coe_relativeAlexanderGrading_eq w, (hD.add hE).coe_relativeAlexanderGrading_eq w,
    ← QuotientAddGroup.mk_add, Pi.add_apply, Pi.add_apply]
  congr 1
  ring

/-- The relative Alexander grading is antisymmetric modulo the periodic multiplicities:
`A(y) - A(x) = -(A(x) - A(y))` for generators joined by a domain. -/
theorem IsDomainBetween.coe_relativeAlexanderGrading_swap (w : Basepoint)
    (hD : H.IsDomainBetween x y D) :
    (H.relativeAlexanderGrading w z y x : ℤ ⧸ H.periodicMultiplicities z) =
      -(H.relativeAlexanderGrading w z x y : ℤ ⧸ H.periodicMultiplicities z) := by
  rw [hD.coe_relativeAlexanderGrading_eq w, hD.neg.coe_relativeAlexanderGrading_eq w,
    ← QuotientAddGroup.mk_neg, Pi.neg_apply, Pi.neg_apply]
  congr 1
  ring

/-- A generator has relative Alexander grading zero with itself. -/
@[simp]
theorem relativeAlexanderGrading_self (w : Basepoint) (hP : ∀ P ∈ H.periodicDomains, P z = 0) :
    H.relativeAlexanderGrading w z x x = 0 := by
  simp [(isDomainBetween_zero x).relativeAlexanderGrading_eq w hP]

/-- The relative Alexander grading is additive, `A(x) - A(y) + (A(y) - A(v)) = A(x) - A(v)` for
generators joined by domains, when every periodic domain vanishes at `z`. -/
theorem IsDomainBetween.relativeAlexanderGrading_add (w : Basepoint)
    (hP : ∀ P ∈ H.periodicDomains, P z = 0) (hD : H.IsDomainBetween x y D)
    (hE : H.IsDomainBetween y v E) :
    H.relativeAlexanderGrading w z x y + H.relativeAlexanderGrading w z y v =
      H.relativeAlexanderGrading w z x v := by
  rw [hD.relativeAlexanderGrading_eq w hP, hE.relativeAlexanderGrading_eq w hP,
    (hD.add hE).relativeAlexanderGrading_eq w hP, Pi.add_apply, Pi.add_apply]
  ring

/-- The relative Alexander grading is antisymmetric, `A(y) - A(x) = -(A(x) - A(y))` for
generators joined by a domain, when every periodic domain vanishes at `z`. -/
theorem IsDomainBetween.relativeAlexanderGrading_swap (w : Basepoint)
    (hP : ∀ P ∈ H.periodicDomains, P z = 0) (hD : H.IsDomainBetween x y D) :
    H.relativeAlexanderGrading w z y x = -H.relativeAlexanderGrading w z x y := by
  rw [hD.relativeAlexanderGrading_eq w hP, hD.neg.relativeAlexanderGrading_eq w hP,
    Pi.neg_apply, Pi.neg_apply]
  ring

/-- **The hat differential respects the Alexander filtration.** A domain counted by the hat
differential of the region system from `x` to `y` is nonnegative and avoids the basepoint `w`,
so `A(x) - A(y) = n_z(D) ≥ 0`, when every periodic domain vanishes at `z`. The differential of
the associated graded complex `CFK̂`, whose homology is `HFK̂`, keeps only the domains that also
avoid `z`, which preserve the Alexander grading. -/
theorem relativeAlexanderGrading_nonneg_of_mem_hatDomains [Fintype Point] [DecidableEq Region]
    [Fintype Region] {χ : Region → ℤ} (w : Basepoint) (hP : ∀ P ∈ H.periodicDomains, P z = 0)
    (hD : D ∈ H.hatDomains χ x y) : 0 ≤ H.relativeAlexanderGrading w z x y := by
  obtain ⟨hD, hw, hD0, -⟩ := mem_hatDomains_iff.mp hD
  rw [hD.relativeAlexanderGrading_eq w hP, hw w, sub_zero]
  exact hD0 z

end HeegaardRegionSystem

end TauCeti
